<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95322" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῦλον</span></b> , τό, mostly in
		pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῦλα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>arms stripped off a slain enemy, spoils</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1428
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1431
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				74
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1000
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.134
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				61
			</span></i> (Olympia, <span class="entity">v B.C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῦλα
				γράφειν</span> to write one's name on <i>arms gained as
				spoils</i>, which were then dedicated to a deity, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				574
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῦλ᾽ ἔδειξα Βακχίῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cyc.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.57
			</span></i>: less freq. in sg., <i>booty, spoil, prey</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῦλον οἰωνοῖσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					897
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.</u>
				620
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.Chr.
				64.24
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς πτέρυγας . . τῇ Νίκῃ φορεῖν
					ἔδοσαν, . . σκῦλον ἀπὸ τῶν πολεμίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristopho
					11.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῦλον τὴν ὑπατείαν φέρεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Mar.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
